sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-13> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.53" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.525"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.56"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "A no-transposition rule is empirically sharp once parts are homologized independently of their connections. Public anatomy ontologies and specimen repositories cover vertebrate skeletons much better than the full list of organ systems in the claim. Turning those sources into a class-wide connectivity test is months of coding, so only a subset can be resolved with what is already structured." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Represent homologous parts as connectivity graphs and test whether, within a class, adjacency order stays fixed while shape and size vary, using gene expression or developmental identity as the homology criterion. The claim is confirmed if transpositions of connection are absent across tetrapod limbs, arthropod limbs and floral organs, and refuted by well-supported reversals of anatomical order." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Homology has often been defined by conserved connections, so a purely anatomical test can become circular.", "Connectivity is coded in an ontology for vertebrate anatomy and is not a downloadable comparative matrix for insect mouthparts, crustacean limbs and flowers together.", "Digit identity shifts and homeotic floral changes require an agreed homology standard before they count as transpositions." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-13 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-13> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-13--grok--operationalizability> .
